{"kind":"event","event_id":1992,"event_uid":"01M2HC6RBJEAJBWC3TP5G58J8W","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":113,"issue_uid":"01M2HBYNCVGT24JHB5G397RBRC","issue_short_id":"rbrc","actor":"exam:1@run-132","hlc_physical_ms":1789437108594,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"e398c087459bbb5e2972f3ed35602e4e3cf9c9a13b6c1959f67291cf7f00b11e","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2HC6RBHYXQN1CHA18RM04S7","author":"exam:1@run-132","body":"examiner (task 1): approach for the exam at fleet/tests/test_run_engine_kata_close.mjs.\n\nOne two-task sim carries legs (a) and (b): waves [[task 1, task 2]], stamp `run-12`, a fake hub of the shape test_worker_kata_env.mjs builds (getIssue/claim/patchMetadata/comment/close/addLabel over an in-memory store, every call recorded in order with the revision it answered), record naming tasks 1 and 2 at the store's revisions. Stub: impl writes its file and returns doneImpl; the reviewer PASSes task 1 and returns a blocking FIX_REQUIRED for task 2 on every round — so task 1 is the wave's one mergeable row and task 2 ends unadopted and needs-review, whether the engine's fix loop is one round or two.\n\n(a) [M1]: among U-1's patchMetadata calls exactly one carries `work.adopted_run`, its patch deep-equals {'work.adopted_run': 12, 'work.adopted_sha': <headSha>} (integer 12, not '12'; sha from the run's `driver:wave-adopted` event in events.jsonl), its revision argument is the revision the fake last answered for U-1 before that call, and the next call for U-1 is the `close`, whose commit evidence deep-equals {type: 'commit', sha: <the same headSha>}.\n(b) [M2]: the fake's store for U-2 has neither adopted key (and no patchMetadata for U-2 ever carried one) while it does carry work.attention 'needs-human'.\n(c) [M3]: the same two-task run built with no kata and no kataRecord — a second fake constructed and never passed records zero calls, no `kata:` event is on the log, and the wave still adopts.\n(d) [M4]: CONTRACT.md read through the Proof's own sed range (the `Kata record (engine)` line through the first `status.json:` line), asserting the Closes sentence names work.adopted_run then work.adopted_sha.\n\nThe exam calls `_engine_helpers.rig` with `kata`, which is the rig edit this task makes; at BASE the rig drops it, the engine's kataOn stays false and (a) is red on the absent patch.","created_at":"2026-09-15T01:51:48.593070259Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T01:51:48.594Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":1993,"event_uid":"01M2HC7V6EVXYVCMXKEBDWKJP3","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":113,"issue_uid":"01M2HBYNCVGT24JHB5G397RBRC","issue_short_id":"rbrc","actor":"impl:1@run-132","hlc_physical_ms":1789437144270,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"b9a9667fe60da71ced250611b8e78620d3dd0956023d9e8ff92f76619c8cbe80","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2HC7V6DWEHW4ARVZ1586B3K","author":"impl:1@run-132","body":"Task 1 done at 99df99bb. The patch is a kataAdopted(id, sha) helper beside kataClose in fleet/run-engine.mjs: same row + kataClosed guard the close reads, drainKataPosts first, then one kataCall('metadata', …) with exactly {'work.adopted_run', 'work.adopted_sha'} under kataRevisions.get(uid) — so the patch and the close are adjacent calls on the uid with nothing between them. Called from the wave loop immediately before kataClose with merge.headSha, the same sha the close's commit evidence carries. The run integer is Number(String(stamp).replace(/^run-/, '')) with a Number.isFinite guard, so stamp 'sim' writes null, never NaN. kataMark (needs-review) untouched, so M2 follows structurally. Rig edit is the agreed one: kata = undefined param plus ...(kata === undefined ? {} : { kata }). Verified all four legs against a scratch sim outside the tree (a fake hub of the test_worker_kata_env shape, run-12, task 2 blocked into needs-review): U-1's call order is getIssue, claim, patchMetadata, close; the patch is exactly the two keys at the wave-adopted headSha; U-2's store carries work.attention needs-human and neither key; the no-kata run folds with zero calls. All six fleet/tests/test_run_engine_*.mjs, test_worker_kata_env.mjs and test_sims_are_hermetic.mjs are green.","created_at":"2026-09-15T01:52:24.269444755Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T01:52:24.27Z"}
