{"kind":"event","event_id":1995,"event_uid":"01M2HC83H61ARA5483ACBQV5QE","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":113,"issue_uid":"01M2HBYNCVGT24JHB5G397RBRC","issue_short_id":"rbrc","actor":"engine:run-132","hlc_physical_ms":1789437152806,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"053b40d1286f27916f282ea0a9c4ccf68c2a2880bc664aff64d3702442d94c71","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2HC83H5DZ8JM8ZT9RGK75J1","author":"engine:run-132","body":"{\"kind\":\"worker:end\",\"label\":\"impl:1\",\"role\":\"implementer\",\"sessionId\":\"1c5431ab-e2bf-44e3-ae82-7bc5a8acecc3\",\"exitCode\":0,\"timedOut\":false,\"outcome\":\"ok\",\"class\":\"success\",\"status\":null,\"meter\":{\"input\":50,\"output\":17878,\"cacheRead\":1403125,\"cacheCreation\":43457,\"costUsd\":1.5833324999999998,\"models\":[\"claude-opus-5\"]},\"id\":\"01M2HC83F10000N4SACQPCGM95\",\"ts\":1789437152737}","created_at":"2026-09-15T01:52:32.805222598Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T01:52:32.806Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":1996,"event_uid":"01M2HC83R2KNX3WRBED5GMXG4W","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":114,"issue_uid":"01M2HBZAE0SJZ2XHW5S6TK8YT2","issue_short_id":"8yt2","actor":"impl:2@run-132","hlc_physical_ms":1789437153026,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"cdd3ae0e7c2b1ac10a0ee256088037e754f5c228112c82e216ee9115b62c7851","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2HC83R0B350XAZJSRP5YPH9","author":"impl:2@run-132","body":"Task 2 (re-drive reuse) approach: (1) lift the per-task getIssue out of runTaskInner into a setup-time loop (openKataTask), keeping the kataOpened guard so the count stays one per task; (2) after that loop, before the baseline clone is cut, compute the reused set (issue status closed + work.adopted_run + work.adopted_sha) and, when non-empty and single-run, fetch ultra/evidence/run-<M>, read report.json + publish-fold/run.patch into runDir/reuse/, fold them through the kernel at --wave 0 with --base report.baseSha and --patch main=<baseSha..BASE diff> --patch reuse=<run.patch>, materialize onto BASE, reset integ to the candidate; (3) baseline clone is cut at BASE and re-anchored onto the reuse head so the baseline suite measures the tree every wave builds on; (4) waveBaseSha starts at the reuse head, the wave-1 clone re-anchor fires when waveBaseSha!==baseSha (not only w>0), reused ids are excluded from runnable and get a done/reused result row in taskResults (NOT the per-wave results array, so an all-reused wave takes the 'merge skipped' continue and not the cascade break), and go into kataClaimed/kataClosed so no hub write touches them. One driver:reuse event either way.","created_at":"2026-09-15T01:52:33.024732151Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T01:52:33.026Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":1997,"event_uid":"01M2HC8BP9NAYMJ4D018XPXXXK","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":113,"issue_uid":"01M2HBYNCVGT24JHB5G397RBRC","issue_short_id":"rbrc","actor":"engine:run-132","hlc_physical_ms":1789437161161,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"0875fddb21abc148978e07d5e9fda942effc5bc89036fa344d2845e3c660daa0","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2HC8BP7YVHEBQ9JFH99FWWA","author":"engine:run-132","body":"{\"kind\":\"driver:attention\",\"task\":\"1\",\"attention\":\"needs-human\",\"msg\":\"session ended without hand-off\",\"actor\":\"\",\"id\":\"01M2HC8BNJ0000K1NT7Q89EXD2\",\"ts\":1789437161138}","created_at":"2026-09-15T01:52:41.159826714Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T01:52:41.161Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":1998,"event_uid":"01M2HCB7HC84D6FCDKW23Q4NN3","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":114,"issue_uid":"01M2HBZAE0SJZ2XHW5S6TK8YT2","issue_short_id":"8yt2","actor":"exam:2@run-132","hlc_physical_ms":1789437255212,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"e56f497dd9c52a940de5367dd4884b713a9042aa317483dba43cd01bd53f5496","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2HCB7HBVVXG9D3DKFMSPQT0","author":"exam:2@run-132","body":"examiner (task 2, reuse): writing fleet/tests/test_run_engine_reuse.mjs now. Approach: a local rig copy in the exam (the test_worker_kata_env.mjs precedent) that adds two things _engine_helpers.rig does not expose — `kata` passed to runEngine and a RECORDING `exec` wrapper around execSeam, because legs (b), (d) and (e) are assertions about what the exec seam recorded (the tag fetch, the kernel's --wave 0 call, the check.sh invocations). The sim origin is built once: P0 = makeRepo's base commit (= the parked run's report.baseSha), an evidence commit tagged ultra/evidence/run-9 carrying .ultrapowers/runs/9/report.json and .../publish-fold/run.patch (task 1's diff against P0, git diff --binary --full-index --no-renames), a side commit for the ancestry refusal tagged ultra/evidence/run-7, then main advanced with third.txt — that tip is the run's BASE, so M5's 'BASE moved past the parked base' is the DEFAULT shape and legs (b), (c) and (e) all read one run. Nine engine runs: 3 for (a), 1 for (b)+(c)+(e), 1 for (c)'s second layout, 4 for (d).","created_at":"2026-09-15T01:54:15.211034877Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T01:54:15.212Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":1999,"event_uid":"01M2HCBMSEW5EW815MKPRCXCKR","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":113,"issue_uid":"01M2HBYNCVGT24JHB5G397RBRC","issue_short_id":"rbrc","actor":"exam:1@run-132","hlc_physical_ms":1789437268782,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"ab6c750ed5d81a3e98779bfacc0858edd21e9005197ecb5169afffb4475ea11f","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2HCBMSDM1EHXFZ2RMNSGZAE","author":"exam:1@run-132","body":"examiner (task 1): exam handed in — fleet/tests/test_run_engine_kata_close.mjs, all four legs live, nothing else in the tree.\n\nRed at BASE for one reason: the preconditions all pass (the two-task sim runs end to end, wave 1 adopts task 1, task 2 ends not-done), and the first failure is `(a) [M1] the engine patched task 1's issue with \\`work.adopted_run\\` exactly once … recorded for U-1 were: []` — at BASE `_engine_helpers.rig` drops the `kata` argument, so `kataOn` is false and no hub call is made at all.\n\nVerified satisfiable: against a scratch copy of the tree carrying the minimal implementation (rig's `kata = undefined` + spread, one `kataCall('metadata', …)` before each `kataClose` in the mergeable loop, the CONTRACT Closes sentence) the exam is green, three runs in a row, and the Proof's `Run:` grep is green on that sentence. It also stays green when the patch is written WITHOUT a `drainKataPosts()` ahead of it, so leg (a)'s \"immediately followed by that uid's close\" and its revision reading do not pin one particular drain placement.\n\nTwo readings a later session would otherwise have to reconstruct:\n- \"under the revision the fake last answered for that uid\" is asserted from outside as: walk the fake's call log to the stamping patch, take the revision of the last answer the fake gave for that uid before it. Reads (getIssue, the attention poll) do not bump the store, so a stray poll cannot move it.\n- \"immediately followed by that uid's close\" is asserted on that UID's OWN call subsequence (`forUid(uid)`), not the global log: comments for the RUN issue may interleave globally, and the leg is about what the engine does to the task's issue.\n\nLeg (b) is asserted twice over — the store for U-2 has neither key, and no patchMetadata for U-2 ever carried one — so a per-key-merge implementation that stamped the wrong issue cannot hide. Nothing is unsatisfiable.","created_at":"2026-09-15T01:54:28.781719577Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T01:54:28.782Z"}
